{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight","id":1557447,"title":"V5's Gehenna: A Serious Oversight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-10T06:09:37-08:00","id":1557447,"title":"V5's Gehenna: A Serious Oversight","content":"Alright, am I the only person who saw a problem with how effortlessly the Tremere and Giovanni got dealt with after the 5th edition Gehenna reboot? I don't just mean in the sense that these were (arguably) popular clans, and shattering them was a bitter pill. I mean in the sense of a narrative context.<br /> <br /> Because I don't think the writers fully realize just what kind of precedent they've set going forward with this. They've effectively demonstrated that the Sabbat actually have a viable plan for the future. Seek out the Antedeluvians, slay them, reign over the night eternal.<br /> <br /> It can't be that hard, after all. The Second Inquisition managed to take down two of them with some drone strikes, and Interpol agents. So an army of mass embraced Shovelheads hopped up on Potence / Celerity should make short work of them!<br /> <br /> <br /> And yes, I know that Giovanni was technically a 3.5th generation, but Tremere had the soul of Tremere, Saulot, and a piece of The Eldest inside him. So combined with Ravnos, that's at least 4 dead Antes that the Sabbat didn't even have to lift a finger for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 01-10-2026, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-10T06:39:47-08:00","id":1557448,"title":"","content":"V5's plot mostly exists for railroading the game to were the writters want it to be rather than on its own merits so these sort of issues are common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-10T13:51:56-08:00","id":1557456,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557448#post1557448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5's plot mostly exists</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait<br /> V5 have a plot that actually exist - even if it is just mostly?<br /> <br /> I mean it is a but retcon...ish<br /> <br /> According to V5 lore, in 2001, a week after 9/11, Homeland Security raids the haven of Jalan-Aajav - Seraph of the Black Hand and one of the most feared warriors within the Sabbat, the Sabbat version of Karsh (I'm in the camp of those who belive Jalan-Aajav and Karsh are the result of the usage of the Dual Form or they are the same individual)- and killed him<br /> This is considered the first recorded attack by what will later be termed the Second Inquisition.<br /> [5th Edition Corebook]<br /> <br /> In 2002 Admiral John Poindexter took control of the Information Awareness Office and greenlighted a number of DARPA initiatives intended to help expose and combat supernatural threats.<br /> <br /> 2003 was the year of the countermove, the Camarilla fed information about the Sabbat to government agencies and used them to help burn out the Camarilla's rival sect and partially thanks to Camarilla manipulations the United States Congress officially defunded the IAO - Roberto Farrier, the hand-picked successor of Admiral Poindexter continued and accelerated the work his mentor started, just under the table. [V5 Camarilla, Second Inquisition, Hunter: The Reckoning 5th Edition]<br /> <br /> In 2004 the National Security Agency discovered and hacked SchreckNET. The Second Inquisition officially formed.<br /> The Red Question first issued a political tractate online named Anarchs Unbound, a New Manifesto for the Digital Age. The tractate was intended as a response to the Anarch Manifesto of Salvador Garcia, using a great variety of mortal theories ranging from Rousseau to Descartes, from Marx to Adam Smith, from Saul Alinsky to Ayn Rand, in order to apply them to the Kindred condition. The text was sent to Anarchs known for dissatisfaction with their Elders<br /> Meanwhile after the Ankaran Sarcophagus crisis in Los Angeles, Isaac Abrams, &quot;Nines&quot; Rodriguez, and Therese Voerman each recognize the other as baron over the respective domains of Hollywood, Downtown, and Santa Monica, agreeing to work together as a council to re-solidify Anarch sovereignty over the city.<br /> <br /> 2005 was probably when the Sabbat begun the slow migration to the middle east that will be known as the Gehenna Crusade. Sabbat cities slowly emptied out over the span of the next decade<br /> <br /> 2006 was the year when thew Anarch vs Camarilla situation started to heat up, this year Anarchs Unbound was officially banned by the Camarilla, and dire warnings were issued about sect members mingling with the Red Question and Camarilla Elders begun to feed information about Anarch holdings as well Sabbat in an attempt to deflect attention from their own domains.<br /> The Camarilla's scheme\u200bs a bit backfired and ended up in the Second Inquisition's offensive in the UK and for seven or so years they started &quot;the sterilization of London&quot;<br /> It is a good question how deeply Mithras was involed, considering he was never the big fan of the Camarilla to begin with and it was a possibility he simply step forward and makes his Domain and &quot;independent&quot; state from the Camarilla, effectively an Anarch Freestate-situation (paired with the high possibility of Vitel's returning and doing the same with his domain this was basically the Camarilla's worst nightmare - so while many label whats happened in London and in the UK as the Camarilla's &quot;mistake&quot; it is totally possible the Inner Circle was totally well aware what they were doing and tried to eliminate that uncomfortable possibility; again proving the SI is/was nothing more than a tool in the Elders'/Camarilla's arsenal)<br /> <br /> 2007 saw two major events<br /> First several young vampires began to sympathize with the Red Question and its ideals and the group addressed the Justicars of the Camarilla directly.<br /> In response to the persecution, they would exact retribution. Only one night later, the Great Recession had begun. T<br /> o mortals, the crisis was the foreseeable consequence of greed, lack of regulation, and simple stupidity. The Camarilla, however, apparently discovered traces of hacking in several of the concerned banks, as well as evidence of Dominate and other disciplines used against CEOs. The Camarilla investigators believe that the Red Question must have spent years prepping for the financial panic they triggered, but to the elder Camarilla leaders who are largely ignorant of the processes involved, it appears as though the Red Question simply flipped a switch and incinerated most of their stock portfolios.<br /> The Camarilla reacted by issuing that the right to judge individual Anarchs would be the matter of the local prince, but that Anarchs Unbound was no greater threat for the sect, merely the work of a coterie of malcontent troublemakers. Several Elders acquired a superstitious dread of the Red Question and the Internet in general, which opened this particular avenue for the exploration of neonates and ancillae that discovered the use of cyber-warfare against both the Red Question and techno-savvy Sabbat that had the same idea.<br /> Now this is mostly in the V20 Anarchs Unbound, but V5 not really retconned this and kept these events intact<br /> The second is not really an event, more like a lore piece, Marcus Questor, the Division Director of the FBI's Special Affairs Division become the agent in charge of the Special Affairs Division, and his ties to the IAO aid in securing intelligence of the blank body phenomenon.<br /> \u200bUltimately Grenzschutzgruppe 10 - an elite anti-terrorist offshoot of the Federal Police - decimated the vampiric population of Munich. Munich remained their primary base of operations, and they repurposed several warehouses within the Munich Olympiapark into clandestine training areas, forensic labs, and barracks\u200b<br /> The Coalition aka the Five Torches (illicit and covert multinational conspiracy within many intelligence services and the Vatican to hunt Vampires) not really took the GSG 10 seriously, but the Camarilla started to watch them, fearing they might join forces\u200b (Cults of the Blood Gods, V5 Camarilla, Second Inquisition)<br /> <br /> 2008 was when the shit hit the fan<br /> A joint SOCOM task force destroyed the Tremere Prime Chantry, decapitating the Tremere pyramid and purging Vienna of Kindred.<br /> Carna begung her flight across the United States, spreading word of what she has learned from The Book of the Grave War to her followers.<br /> And the Anarchs took the opportunity to conquer several weak Camarilla domains while the Second Inquisition purges the Sabbat stronghold of Montreal in an event known as the &quot;Night of Ashes&quot;.<br /> <br /> In 2009 Mithras made his move and with the help of Roger de Camden basically helped to form Operation Antigen, a Second Inquisition operation enacted to exterminate London Camarilla and Kindred<br /> \u200bMeanwhile Kevin Jackson took the opportunity to declare his own Praxis, becoming Prince of Chicago.<br /> (Fall of London, Chicago by Night 5th Edition)<br /> <br /> 2010 was a minor setback if you will<br /> Honolulu's small Kindred population was completely purged by the IAO, becoming the primary headquarters of the organization. (Hunter: The Reckoning 5th Edition)<br /> <br /> in 2011 the Camarilla Inner Council chose a new slate of Justicars<br /> <br /> 2012 was when some big things happened<br /> Simultaneous conclaves were held in Chicago and Prague. Theo Bell assassinated Hardestadt (and possibly Jan Pieterzoon) at the Prague Conclave.<br /> The Brujah formally left the Camarilla.<br /> Juggler - a Brujah, who has been a pain in the Chicago Camarilla\u2019s ass and a thorn in Modius\u2019s side for the better part of a century - surreptitiously produced a Hollywood zombie movie filmed in Gary, Indiana. The film was heavily coded with pro-Anarch messages. The Anarchs of Hollywood recognized his handiwork, and back his claim to become the Baron of Gary.<br /> A group of Kindred led by an infiltrator compromised Second Inquisition operations in the Midwest across three states, disrupting a city-clearing operation in Detroit.<br /> The Heralds of the Sun (a coterie of Kindred modified through ritual to serve as perfect vessels of Mithras's will) were awakened by the Cult of Mithras to help prepare their Methuselah god-king for the Ritual of Transferring the Soul.<br /> (Fall of London, Chicago by Night 5th Edition, Let the Streets Run Red, 5th Edition Corebook, V5 Camarilla)<br /> <br /> 2013 marked the end of the sterilization of London when when Queen Ann was decapitated - again, I'm not that sure it was not Mithras who orchastrated the whole thing<br /> The Camarilla met with the Banu Haqim and the Setite Ministry on the same night to weigh the merits of admission into the Camarilla. The Ministry meeting ended prematurely when a bomb levels the hotel where the dignitaries are convening, with the blast reportedly destroyed the Justicar Molly MacDonald.<br /> The meeting with the Banu Haqim resulted in ironing out the detaild of their admittance to the sect (that happened a few years later)<br /> Facing rejection, the Ministry instead moved to align themselves with the Anarchs.<br /> Also this in this year The Camarilla took Mexico City.<br /> (Children of the Blood, V5 Camarilla)<br /> <br /> 2014 was quite, Prince Quentin King disappeared from Boston under mysterious circumstances. While many assumed him to have been Beckoned, in reality, King had been captured and imprisoned by Hilda MacAndrews (the Toreador Primogen of Boston) in retaliation for the humiliation and mutilation she'd suffered on the Prince's orders. (Boston by Night, Vampire: The Masquerade - Swansong)<br /> <br /> 2015 was the same, a mysterious hysteria plagued several members of the Boston Camarilla (a faction of the Camarilla in the New England region of the United States. They were enemies of the British Camarilla, a faction of the Camarilla based in the British Isles - this was a bit of strange since in theory the British Camarilla or London Camarilla was destroyed by the Second Inquisition during Operation Antigen alongside with Queen Anne. BUT, since the British Camarilla was formerly led by Mithras before Anne and Mithras' fate is a bit ambiguous it is possible it reformed quietly under his new rule. Or simply the Boston Camarilla vs. London Camarilla is just an anachronisitic habit and with Operation Antigen eliminating their rival, the Boston Camarilla simply not really accpeted the fact or just remembered the enmity fondly. Not really important at the end of the day, tho' could be the source of games)<br /> (Boston by Night, Fall of London, In Memoriam, Vampire: The Masquerade - Swansong)<br /> <br /> 2016 - nothing as far as I know happened that could be pinned down here<br /> <br /> in 2017 on the other hand a ,assive slaughter in Berlin stretched the Masquerade to the breaking point and Berlin become an Anarch domain after Prince Abraham Wolff is destroyed in the street (V5 Anarch)<br /> <br /> 2018 is initial jumping-off point of the timeline, as of the publication of the V5 Corebook.<br /> Vannevar Thomas claimed praxis over Los Angeles. The city's Anarch barons quickly negotiated a truce with the Camarilla in order to avoid an immediate, highly destructive war.<br /> Antwerp was taken over by the Anarchs after centuries of Camarilla rule weakeining its presence in Belgium; the rebels crushed in the skull of Toreador Prince Delphine Ga\u00ebl, who was trapped in a trance and met Final Death being stuffed into a barrel and burned next to a police barricade.<br /> The Voerman sisters' Asylum franchise has expanded internationally, with nightclubs opening all across America, Asia, and Europe.<br /> The Succubus Club debuted in Los Angeles, with Victoria Ash herself in attendance. The evening is finished out with Baron Victor Temple publicly executing his rival Bobby Blaine on the dance floor.<br /> The Banu Haqim formally joined the Camarilla.<br /> \u200b<br /> In 2019 Clan Lasombra is granted formal membership in the Camarilla after a vote in Chicago, following a diplomatic campaign by the Amici Noctis.<br /> The torpored body of Zelios (from Transylvania by Night series) was discovered in a labyrinth hidden deep within the sewers beneath Griffith Park in Los Angeles. He was eventually recovered and awakened by Maximillian Strauss<br /> Baron Isaac Abrams of Hollywood left Los Angeles to answer the Beckoning.<br /> The Odenses Pact and the ceremonial Vermilion Wedding between Victoria Ash and Tegyrius cemented the alliance between the Camarilla and the Ashirra.\u200b<br /> Chaz Price, the Herald of Prince Vannevar Thomas was destroyed by the Anarchs, triggering a war between them and the Camarilla for control of Los Angeles.<br /> <br /> 2020 was again &quot;noisy&quot;<br /> A devastating Second Inquisition offensive, spearheaded by the Society of Leopold, roiled the vampiric population of Los Angeles. The Camarilla, finding the situation untenable, withdrawed from the city once more as Prince Vannevar Thomas and his court abandoned the city.<br /> The L.A. Anarchs quickly regrouped and attacked the Society, decapitating their leadership and crippling their operations in the city.<br /> Victorious in the moment, they redeclared the sovereignty of the Anarch Free State and pronounce the Camarilla persona non grata.<br /> <br /> 2021<br /> Justicar Ian Carfax was destroyed by Lupines.<br /> (Winter's Teeth, Crimson Thaw)<br /> Reports circulated of a brutal civil war in Brazil between the Sabbat and Thin-blooded followers of the Path of the Sun.<br /> <br /> 2022<br /> A blood cult known as the Cult of Aristovoros begun to cause turmoil within the city of Athens. However, it's later revealed that the cult was little more than an elaborate ploy by Sophia Komnenou to seize power from the reigning Prince Peisistratos.<br /> (Vampire: The Masquerade - Sins of the Sires)<br /> <br /> 2023<br /> A coterie was assembled by the Camarilla Court of Montreal in order to investigate rumors of the Sabbat's resurgence within the city.<br /> \u200b(Vampire: The Masquerade - CHAPTERS)<br /> <br /> \u200b2024<br /> Theo Bell and Agata Starek wiped out a Sabbat nest in Belfast.<br /> The Plague-Bride - a legendary 4th Generation methuselah of the Malkavians who was the handmaiden of Malkav himself, who soothed him in his fervors and cooled his forehead. was sighted - in a small village in Romania.<br /> This is an interesting lorepiece, since the Plague-Bride was also counted among the Coronati \u2013 those of Malkav's childer who devoured the vitae-laced earth where Malkav was rendered apart during the uprising of the Third Generation in order to preserve him and spread his madness<br /> \u200b\u200b(Gehenna War)<br /> <br /> 2025<br /> As I said above, the Plague-Bride's return was interesting?<br /> Why?<br /> Because this year Kali (California Lowenthal, the childe of the infamous Reynard Casse) managed to flee New York in possession of a vial containing the vitae of the Ravnos Antediluvian.<br /> (Vampire: The Masquerade - Reckoning of New York)<br /> <br /> <br /> Now these are all fun little things and all, but V5 while have some form of coherent time line built on V20 mostly do have some questions<br /> <br /> <b>When the Followers of Set changed name?</b><br /> At some point following the start of Gehenna, the clan underwent a name change, now identifying themselves as the Ministry, save for those in Africa or of Egyptian descent, who still use the old name. In part it was a rebranding, an update for the times, but it was also a sign that the clan's understanding of its relationship to its founder had changed \u2013 rather than being Set's followers, they see Set as being within them, making them his living church.<br /> Now... in V5? Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition reframed Gehenna significantly, changing it to the Gehenna War<br /> It is a bit weird but... okay<br /> <br /> <b>When the Beconing started?</b><br /> \u200bNo one really knows, but Elders, such as the Nosferatu Calebros, started feeling the Beckoning in 2014.<br /> <br /> <b>When the Gehenna War started?</b><br /> Not long after the Beckoning... or the two intertwined.<br /> <br /> <b>When the Hecata was formed?</b><br /> Good question. An attack on Giovanni holdings in Venice by the Harbingers, the release of wraiths and spectres caused by the death (or incapacitation and disappearance) of Augustus Giovanni, and by rumors of the Promise of 1528 coming to an end in 2028 and severla other factors led to the negotiations between the parties resulted in the formation of the new Clan of Death, Clan Hecata. So...<br /> ...so it is basically impossible to pinpoint. BUT maybe around... 2010? Because of the last question<br /> <br /> <b>When Augustus Giovanni was... destroyed?</b><br /> Now the thing is it is not 100% Augustus bit the dust.<br /> As of the late 2010s, Augustus Giovanni was no longer active in the clan organization. His fate, if he has met it, is unknown; he might be dead or diablerized (the list of possible suspects is long), on the run, or imprisoned somewhere. In any case, the host of wraiths and spectres controlled by him were unleashed on the world, in part leading to the Family Reunion and the formation of Clan Hecata. (Nor Tattered Fa\u00e7ade, neither Trails of Ash and Bone nor Cults of the Blood Gods offered a good explanation; a returning theme of V5)<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T01:06:45-08:00","id":1557463,"title":"","content":"I felt the urge to pull my jaw over my face with that compilation lol. Its so bad and very obviously their for soft retcons and railroading","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 01-11-2026, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T03:32:07-08:00","id":1557464,"title":"","content":"The whole Ministry thing is one of my pet peeves (and trust me I have many!) when it comes to V5 &quot;soft retcons and railroading&quot;<br /> Lets put aside the rebranding, because Clans are tend to do that and the Followers of Set was technically how the others called them, they tend to refer themselves as the Mesu Bedshet - Children of Rebellion<br /> <br /> What annoyed me in this soft retcon was the fact the Followers of Set were invited by the Camarilla in the XV century, during the Convention of Thorns but they politely refused the offer at the moment - something that is rumored made Raphael de Corazon upset - and prefered to remain Independent<br /> <br /> Reportedly a Nosferatu spy discovered the location of Alamut sometime during the Anarch Revolt but the Followers tell another tale; according to them while they played both sides, supporting the Elders of Eupre and the Anarch movement equally everything changed when the Assamites entered the fray - the Followers and the Assamites had a long history of bad blood and that made them side with the Elders against the Anarchs and at the end they were the one who provided the location of Alamut for the Camarilla to siege that forced them to the talking tables - considering in the Second Baali war Sutekh personally appeared and helped out to blow up Thera with his sorcerers to flood Crete it is not impossible it is actually true; the Followers of Set when things go South are more than willing to help out against a common enemy<br /> Some says the entire Sect owes the Followers of Set a gigantic, collective Life Boon: the Hierophants of Egypt have the right to demoand <b><i>anything</i></b> from the Inner Circle, once and some even go further saying one Hierophant secretly attend each meeting of the Inner Cricle<br /> <br /> Now how much is it true? Good question. But would explain why Raphael de Corazon was upset when the Followers not joined<br /> <br /> Even if it is not true, the original invitation never expired, the Followers of Set could have joined any time<br /> Anyhow, abandoning their literally several millenia long neutrality to join the Anarchs of all organizations was hard to swallow ant not really made sense - even tho' the Banu Haqim also tried to join in the same time and they had a bad blood, the situation was different than the Revolt's<br /> <br /> Nakhthorheb, also known as the First Son, is the leader of the Hierophants of the Followers of Set during the Dark Ages. Rumors say that he was born into the same nomad tribe as Set himself and was among the first to receive the Embrace from the Antediluvian (making him well over 10K years old and just a few years younger than Sutekh himself)<br /> He was also known for his distrust against foreigners and his adamant refusal to Embrace non-Egyptians into the Clan. He spent much of his time wandering through the wastes of Lower Egypt, planning how the make Egypt strong again.<br /> He later fell into torpor and has yet to awaken in the Final Nights. Rumor says that he now sleeps in the House of Set, a Founding Temple located in Uganda near Lake Victoria (according Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom)<br /> Now what we have here is a 4th Generation direct Childe of Sutekh, hating <i>everything</i> not Egyptian, especially non-Egyptian Followers of Set.<br /> It would have been so easy, so logical to make him wake up, look around and start a massive purge of the Clan like Ur-Shulgi<br /> Nakhthorheb was the greatest of the Hierophants; it was he who held the Hierophants in an iron grip. While all laws and commands given had to be agreed upon by all seven elders, it was Nakhthorheb who was the source of these commands<br /> Before Sutekh's disappearance in 33 AD the Followers of Set had no ral organization. What their God commanded they did it and he sat on the top of the food chain. Once their god went missing, the Hierophants came together and declared themselves the stewards of the clan - led by Nakhthorheb<br /> He already restructured the whole Clan\u2026 after awakening in the 21th Century, looking around and not likeing what he saw going out full Baba Yaga or Ur-Shulgi would have been logical, presenting a similar situation the Banu Haqim were in and we could have a traditional &quot;orthodox&quot; Clan lead by Nakhthorheb and the rest who fled in the Camarilla - heck there were already Setites in the Camarilla!!! They were just not represented by a Justicar. One was even an Archon and Guide to the Camarilla had several tips and information on how to use the Setites in the Camarilla<br /> Armed with the ancient Settite Sorcery, Akhu, and the mystical knowledge (even breaking the monopoly of the necromancers, since they have a nice extended knowledge of the Underworld) they could have been easly the &quot;new Tremere&quot; replacing them as &quot;court magicians and advisors&quot;...<br /> <br /> Alas this ship has sailed<br /> <br /> But still this was one of the biggest retcon and idiotic move V5 came up with on par with the Samedi suddenly &quot;getting better&quot; after an unlife spent as rotting corpses and the Harbringers regrew their faces\u2026<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T05:00:10-08:00","id":1557466,"title":"","content":"It's my understanding that the rebranding of the Setites is also something that the clan desperately needed. Not from the stand point of how silly a clan of chaos worshipers in the modern nights had become, but in the sense that the entire clan had effectively become a bunch of heretics.<br /> <br /> <br /> Set believed that by spreading chaos and violating taboos, you could break free of the shackles of the false gods and transcend to a higher state of existence. But at some point down the line, his followers either forgot this message, or distorted it into a religion that was about spreading chaos purely for its own sake. They forgot what Set stood for, which is why he was so furious with them after waking up from Torpor during Gehenna.<br /> <br /> <br /> The soft retcon sounds more in line with what Set was originally trying to achieve, instead of what the clan ended up devolving into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T09:24:07-08:00","id":1557470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557464#post1557464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But still this was one of the biggest retcon and idiotic move V5 came up with on par with the Samedi suddenly &quot;getting better&quot; after an unlife spent as rotting corpses and the Harbringers regrew their faces\u2026<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Probably for the same reason why the Nosferatu got remodeled to look like a bunch of people with skin diseases and congenital birth defects, instead of the masquerade shattering monsters they were before. Or why Vicissitude is a pale shadow of its former glory.<br /> <br /> 5th edition seems to have wanted to scale down / dial back on the overtly monstrous aspects that existed in previous editions by making all (playable) vampires more in touch with their humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 01-11-2026, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T11:46:52-08:00","id":1557473,"title":"","content":"5th always wanted to copy some of the good aspects of Requiem 2e from the CofD without necessarily thinking about the impact of context for how rules play out.<br /> <br /> Requiem 2e changed the Clan weaknesses so that they scale, and start very weak. This isn't about the &quot;street vs. epic&quot; scope issue. The Requiem developers were pretty clear that they wanted being a vampire to be &quot;sexy&quot; for awhile. Newly Embraced vampires seem to be a ton of bonuses with few penalties. It's only over time that the costs start to set in. It's only long since a vampire has completely accepted their new condition and started to justify the necessity of certain immoral actions to continue their unlives, that vampires start to really get hit with the &quot;curse&quot; side of things.<br /> <br /> V5 copied the idea of scaling weaknesses, but didn't really tie it into the thematic thrust of the game the way Requiem did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T16:00:43-08:00","id":1557485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557473#post1557473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 copied the idea of scaling weaknesses, but didn't really tie it into the thematic thrust of the game the way Requiem did.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also messed up some of the weaknesses, like making the Nosferatu have the compulsion to seek out information. That's not something that was part of their clan curse, it was a defense mechanism against the Niktuku. Why the hell does The Beast care about find out somebody's social security number, or the precise number of chicken wings they ate within a given year? The Beast is a creature of blind instinct and primal impulse<br /> <br /> <br /> Likewise, the Setite's compulsion to violate the game's tenets deconstructs the entire premise of them being a cult in the first place. You don't need to subject somebody to a lengthy indoctrination process. Just embrace them and let The Beast do the work for you. Also, isn't violating the tenets of Humanity kind of the whole concept behind falling to The Beast?<br /> <br /> Which means that the Setite's vampiric weakness is literally just... being a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T19:12:50-08:00","id":1557493,"title":"","content":"You.... really don't need to convince me of V5's faults. I have hundreds of posts on this forum about them. I was simply adding a consideration to how to analyze them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T18:24:40-08:00","id":1557529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557485#post1557485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They also messed up some of the weaknesses, like making the Nosferatu have the compulsion to seek out information. That's not something that was part of their clan curse, it was a defense mechanism against the Niktuku. Why the hell does The Beast care about find out somebody's social security number, or the precise number of chicken wings they ate within a given year? The Beast is a creature of blind instinct and primal impulse<br /> <br /> <br /> Likewise, the Setite's compulsion to violate the game's tenets deconstructs the entire premise of them being a cult in the first place. You don't need to subject somebody to a lengthy indoctrination process. Just embrace them and let The Beast do the work for you. Also, isn't violating the tenets of Humanity kind of the whole concept behind falling to The Beast?<br /> <br /> Which means that the Setite's vampiric weakness is literally just... being a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yep, that's the issue with the compulsion. While the common behavior associated with each clan was a mixture of choice of embrace, clan culture and adaptation to one's curse and powers, now it's compulsive. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T18:29:55-08:00","id":1557531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557529#post1557529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, that's the issue with the compulsion. While the common behavior associated with each clan was a mixture of choice of embrace, clan culture and adaptation to one's curse and powers, now it's compulsive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which makes the whole screening process for clan candidates kind of a waste of energy. Since merely joining the clan will automatically steer you towards upholding their stereotype over time.<br /> <br /> Ventrue WILL demand people acknowledge their authority.<br /> <br /> Brujah WILL seek to tear down the status quo.<br /> <br /> Toreador WILL seek to explore artistic expression.<br /> <br /> Assamites WILL seek to punish wrongdoers.<br /> <br /> So on, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 01-12-2026, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T19:36:24-08:00","id":1557533,"title":"","content":"One of the big issues with the Ministry/Followers of Set is that the clan still hasn't really been explored all that well in V5.<br /> <br /> Traditionally, the Setites were one of the clans that actually had a pretty powerful clan structure, with the clan leadership being composed of a council of ancient millennial old methuselahs and new members being indoctrinated pretty heavily. It wasn't quite on the level of the Tremere, but the Followers had one of the more centralized and unified clan structures. Given their location, when the Beckoning happened, it's likely that many of the leaders within the Followers of Set vanished pretty quickly leaving a big power vacuum at the top, which is what caused the clan to fracture. <br /> <br /> Rather than the split being a rebranding it seems like this would be a full on civil war between different sects of religious fanatics. You have one sect (the Ministry) being iconoclasts claiming that the clan's fundamental understanding of Set has been wrong for thousands and thousands of years, and then you'd have the other sect which would insist on following the traditional teachings about Set. They spent millennia following Set's teaching and literally called themselves the Followers of Set, and now this new faction calling itself the Ministry no longer even pays lip service to the idea of following Set. There's no way that this would be any sort of peaceful separation or a simple rebranding, especially with the clan leadership missing and everyone fighting over their scraps. <br /> <br /> I think there's some really neat conceptual space around the Ministry/Setite split, but it often ends up being kind of head-canony because the game itself hasn't explored any of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T02:31:40-08:00","id":1557540,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight#post1557447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, am I the only person who saw a problem with how effortlessly the Tremere and Giovanni got dealt with after the 5th edition Gehenna reboot?<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition managed to take down two of them with some drone strikes, and Interpol agents. So an army of mass embraced Shovelheads hopped up on Potence / Celerity should make short work of them!<br /> <br /> And yes, I know that Giovanni was technically a 3.5th generation, but Tremere had the soul of Tremere, Saulot, and a piece of The Eldest inside him. So combined with Ravnos, that's at least 4 dead Antes that the Sabbat didn't even have to lift a finger for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now the thing is... no<br /> They don't<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition not even went near Venice to harass Augustus<br /> He went of the map around 2010 - at least the last time he was active in the Clan but his fate, if he has met it, is <b>unknown </b>as I said above<br /> He might be dead or diablerized on the run, or imprisoned somewhere. In any case, the host of wraiths and spectres controlled by him were unleashed on the world, in part leading to the Family Reunion and the formation of Clan Hecata. (Nor Tattered Fa\u00e7ade, neither Trails of Ash and Bone nor Cults of the Blood Gods offered a good explanation; a returning theme of V5) The Hecata waltzed in and took control Venice<br /> <br /> Now Tremere...<br /> Originally Tremere - as Mark Rein-Hagen's personal character in the first games of Ars Magica, not a surprise - always had this weird plot armour and managed to battle Saulot, who had a solid ~10K years behind his back for mental dominance...<br /> It was weird to say the least...<br /> ...but they sold it as Saulot slight miscalulation and Temere's superawesomecool mental powers<br /> V20 on the other hand approached from a different, in that Goratrix was already claimed during the <i>Dark Ages</i> that he was, in fact, Tremre having been forced outside his body after he was possessed by Saulot and that the thing that the Clan served is Saulot either struggling with the Eldest, who gain acces t othe body thanks to the Vicissitude &quot;infection&quot; or Saulot already dual mind, and Saulot the &quot;Noble&quot; /Hun battled with Saulot the Evil /P'o/Beast untill they split phisically and one part &quot;Good Saulot&quot; wandered away and Evil Saulot remained behind as the White Worm of Vienna (to be fair, not a feat, considering the level 2 power of the Cultivation Discipline called Cleave the Demon allows the Kuei-jin separates his P'o from his Hun, leaving the other part of the soul in spirit form... from that materialze the other part is not that hard or find a body...)<br /> In this case, Saulot would have overtaken Tremere <i>immediately</i> - something that make more sense - and would be the force that sent Clan Tremere against the Salubri, joined the Camarilla, and would have defeated Tremere when he destroyed the Tremere antitribu.<br /> Or if you go with the original, In 1999, Tremere fled to the body of his former lover Goratrix, who had long ago defected to the Sabbat. He traveled in Etrius' body to Mexico City, where he manipulated Goratrix into opening himself up to possession. After possessing Goratrix, he attempted to regain his Third Generation status by sacrificing all of the Tremere Antitribu at once to absorb their power.<br /> In V5 Tremere is <i>presumably</i> still occupying the body of Goratrix, and may be the controlling force behind the newly re-emergent House Goratrix<br /> The point is, we... don't really know where the hell Tremere was/is but probably in Goratrix<br /> Now the Second Inquisition indeed cleared out Vienna<br /> In 2008 the Vienna Chantry was assaulted by the forces of the Coalition, with IAO-directed missile strikes leveling three whole city blocks.<br /> It was not a surgical strike, it was a wide spread bombing basically and V20 Companion actually explained the why - the Tremere deliberately cloaked the exact location of the chantry through geomantic rituals and parts of the Chantry are constantly relocated throughout all the city where the body of Tremere lied in Torpor (or the White Worm. Dealers choice)<br /> But here is the thing - the original Tremere clan weakness consisted of an initiation, which required all neonates to drink from the blood of the seven elders of the clan when they are created<br /> Not Tremere's blood<br /> During the <b>Fall of Vienna </b>resulted <i>presumably</i> the destruction of the <u>Inner Council of Seven</u>, Blood Bonds were shattered.<br /> The Tremere fell from gray eminences to personae non gratae in many regions. Without the strict internal hierarchy, individual Tremere compete heavily for the lore, artifacts, and secrets that the united Clan once possessed, fearing their clanmates as much as their enemies. To this end, they often sell their services as mercenaries to third parties. Their former monolithic structure has splintered into several rival groups, with the Camarilla-loyalists under Karl Schrekt at the head on the one side, a resurgent House Goratrix on the other, and the upstarts of House Carna who are at least for the time being still aligned with the Camarilla. A fourth house, Ipsissimus, can be found among the Anarchs.<br /> As for their Antediluvian?<br /> It was never a factor and the Second Inquisition was not even aware there was on in Vienna - or for that matter? Anyone else. Just rumors.<br /> Well except Goratrix and Tremere himself or as a bonus Saulot who god knows where at the moment. And maybe the Eldest. But since the last two are not tied to a body they are off the list - but a good option some of them orchastreted the whole thing playing the SI like a fidle.<br /> If you look closely the Second Inquisition cleared out many - in the eyes of the Camarilla - problematic persons. Or just ended ancient grudges or finished long term plans like with the case of Mithras.<br /> The point is the Sabbat not really knew for certain Tremere bit the dust and there are one less big bad around<br /> Nor the fate of Augustus is common knowledge. Or secret knowledge for thta matter<br /> <br /> From the Sabbat point of view Humans became problematic and killed a bunch of Elders<br /> Witch would be good if the Sabbat wouldn't be an owergrown Anarch branch, based on personal gurdges - and not philosophy<br /> And of course if the upper and middle achelons of the Sabbat hierarchy hadn't been made up of Elders...<br /> The absolute core of the Sabbat was really three coteries: the Conspiracy of Lugoj Blood-Breaker (Sascha, Velya, Lambach, etc.); the Conspiracy of Gratiano de Verontesse (Gratiano, other Lasombra), and the Furies of Tyler (Patricia Bolingbroke). By the Convention of Thorns, these three cores had attracted a good number of ambitious vampires<br /> Now lets put aside, even the fledgelings who helped to found the Sabbat now around 500 years old - the leaders and founders?<br /> Yeah, thick blooded Elders with <i>grudges - every one of them. </i>Myca, Lamback, Velya, Gratioano, Tyler. They simply had enough on the personal level, it was not out of their good heart for a better world....<br /> Lambach, Radu, Velya, Vykos, Rustovich, Mon\u00e7ada... yeah they are Big names and even bigger Elders. Most of them were Elders and old as dust to begin with and since then just got older<br /> Some pretty key reinforcements to the Sabbat came later, the support of the Unconquered (1496); the support of the Black Hand (17th century?); the defection of House Goratrix (18th century); the defection of Melinda Galbraith (17th century)<br /> But those again, were Elders with personal grudges<br /> <br /> The Sabbat have two &quot;confirmed&quot; kills - or at least that is the propaganda<br /> The Eldest is ... you know the story and Lambach actually was very vocal about it - just no one belived him, the Eldest still exist.<br /> The second is the Lasombra Antediluvian. The problem?<br /> Yeah, the Lasombra Antediluvian died, bot got better. in theory he was eaten by a flock of rebels, lead by Grationo... yet - and this is cannon, mind you, not just pulled out my ass - nobody can recall the exact event, and Grationo never claimed the &quot;throne&quot; nor became a 3rd generation vampire. The whole thing is a fuzzy mess in the minds who been there and if that is not the working of a Dominate, nothing is.<br /> All and all, the Lasombra Antediluvian became an Abyssal Entity when he entered the Qlippoth of Primodial Darkness this we, as players know.<br /> <br /> And you know we &quot;seen&quot; something like this before<br /> Or something <i>very</i> similar<br /> After the fall of the Second City, Malkav is believed to have traveled towards the city of Petra. It is along this journey that some think the Eldest Malkavian was attacked and torn asunder. Yet even if his body was destroyed, it is believed that his spirit survived inside of his childer, who gathered at the site of his death and drank his spilled blood, taking Malkav's essence into them and sheltering it from the sun's rays.<br /> (A vampire not fully destroyed untill his Heart's blood is destroyed and if anyone the Children of Haqim know <i>eveything</i> about the Heart&quot;s blood - their studies of vitae have isolated the part within a vampire's blood that contains the soul. They call it &quot;heart's blood&quot; and it manifests as a thick, blackish liquid that quickly grows dry when it leaves the body. Via applications of Quietus they are able to manipulate the heart's blood to allow them to diablerize a victim later. Furthermore, studies in Quietus have found a way to force the last drop of vitae within a vampire's body to calcify the heart into a semi-translucent grayish-white flask known as a &quot;<i>Debitum</i>&quot;. The Debitum enshrouds the spiritual essence (the &quot;heart's-blood&quot;) of the victim \u2013 which, if examined in detail, can be seen encased within, swimming in despair. Heart\u2019s-blood preserved in this way endures indefinitely. (Dark Ages: Vampire Rulebook, p. 209, Vampire Twentieth Anniversary Edition: The Dark Ages, p. 244))<br /> Following this logic with a side tangent, here is that little V5 thing, called:<br /> &quot;<b>Blood of Zapathasura</b>&quot; - Thick, <b>sentient</b> ropes of his vitae stained the ground in Bangladesh where he fell. The noonday sun <b>did not destroy it all</b>. You own a small vial containing the Blood of the Ravnos Antediluvian. What you do with this vitae is up to you, and what it does to anyone who imbibes it is up to the Storyteller.<br /> Funny to think, Zapathasura became Venom-like Anyhow, Malkav survived destruction and became the Madness Network and are inside his Clan... Maybe Zappy pulled a Malkav<br /> And the Lasombra antedulivan did the same mayhaps?<br /> <br /> Now Malkav's case is very similar whats happened with Lasombra - a Group &quot;diablerie&quot; without anyone becoming 3rd gen - just like in the case of the Lasombra Antediluvian's attackers, Gratiano and co.<br /> <br /> Like the True Vessel in Cappadocius and Augustus' case... it could be the Lasombra Antediluvian's &quot;backup plan&quot; or linchpin to the world...<br /> <br /> But okay, lets say the Sabbat killed two, because after all, that is why they managed to get together and get some traction - but in reality, I think even these Elders know, yeah, yikes.<br /> The rest?<br /> Heck even V5 threw in the possiblity Zapatashura not really died<br /> <br /> So in this regard no, V5 handling the events - and trust me it pains me to type this - was actually quite logical<br /> <br /> Like the Tzimisce and the Lasombra jumping shit at the moment the Sabbat - that was nothing more basically just a tool to wage wars against their gurdges - went ballistic and truly commited itself to be the &quot;Sword of Caine&quot; that will destroy the Ancients and Antediluvians. First of all, most of the leadership themselves at the pint sported a hefty 1000 yeras or not more behind their backs and second, most of them suspected the whole Antediluvian-killing was not a great idea to begin with (I mean just take Vykos! They personally gave birth/carried the essence of the Dracon and experienced how hard to kill these things or more like borderline impossible)<br /> As a side note, lots of them were Nodist to begin with and anywone who read the Book of Nod noticed the one thing Caine never was a big fan of is kin-slaying<br /> Heck if you take the Erciyes Fragments he even handed out the Generation-lowering with each Embrace to make sure the younger ones will be ALWAYS weaker than the Older ones... trying to hack and slash your way thrugh his grandchildren, no matther how he hated them was basically against his wishes...<br /> But the main problem with Sabbat was the fact it was never about ideology, it was about grudges and defiance<br /> The moment the Gehenna War the fanatics molded the Sabbat from a comfortable \u201cdo as you like\u201d to a \u201cthose who are not with as are against as\u201d attitude and demanded that every true Sabbat has to march with them in their war against the Antedeluvian and other old vampires and the Sect degenerated basically a mindless swarm of locusts, giving up clan identity, completely turning from humanity, and went to war in full force with the same effectiveness as World War I. tactics of sending wave after wave of soldiers to attack the nigh untouchable Machine Gunners on ridges, the Amici Noctis clearly saw that now was the time to leave and anyone who stayed just proved they lack the survival instinct that defined their Clan - also <i>failed</i> - and the Tzimsice, so attached to their domains and gians fled with them (for some reason to the Anarch and not the neo-feudal Camarilla... but it is a whole different topic)<br /> <br /> And lets be fair most of them never truly been Sabbat if you look closely to begin with - just used it as a power base, ruled/manipulated and took power from it, but payed lip service in large part.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T15:17:53-08:00","id":1557968,"title":"","content":"I personally think it would be fitting that &quot;The Last Supper&quot; in Cult Of The Blood Gods was the ritual consumption of Augustus Giovanni to bind the various necromantic bloodlines together to survive a more dangerous world.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of that the Followers of Set rebranding themselves as the Ministry to be closer to what Set wanted to accomplish in the first place and we are possibly seeing a mini civil war among the clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T17:47:56-08:00","id":1557972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557968#post1557968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the idea of that the Followers of Set rebranding themselves as the Ministry to be closer to what Set wanted to accomplish in the first place and we are possibly seeing a mini civil war among the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Set didn't want to spread chaos just for the sake of chaos. He did it, because he believed it would allow him and others to break free of the false gods' control. Over time, the Setites forgot this goal and degenerated into a bunch of evil hedonists.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Ministry</b> seems to have rediscovered Set's original purpose, whether they're aware of it or not. While the <b>Followers of Set</b> continue to engage in heresy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T19:15:09-08:00","id":1557973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557968#post1557968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think it would be fitting that &quot;The Last Supper&quot; in Cult Of The Blood Gods was the ritual consumption of Augustus Giovanni to bind the various necromantic bloodlines together to survive a more dangerous world.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of that the Followers of Set rebranding themselves as the Ministry to be closer to what Set wanted to accomplish in the first place and we are possibly seeing a mini civil war among the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>This idea looks like V5 modus operandi. Pitch a canon changing sensationalist idea on a book and wait for the replies on the forums. Gather data, publish it and retcon it later on another book leaving it open until a majority of the players/forumites agree on the follow up canon idea.<br /> <br /> Hope its not like that that, but feels like it.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T20:35:56-08:00","id":1557976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557973#post1557973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This idea looks like V5 modus operandi. Pitch a canon changing sensationalist idea on a book and wait for the replies on the forums. Gather data, publish it and retcon it later on another book leaving it open until a majority of the players/forumites agree on the follow up canon idea.<br /> <br /> Hope its not like that that, but feels like it.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how Augustus was blatantly racist, and gave his clan explicit instructions not to embrace certain ethnic groups, I seriously doubt he'd be a willing participant of unifying the various clans of death. Especially in regards to the Samedi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T23:59:15-08:00","id":1557981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557976#post1557976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given how Augustus was blatantly racist, and gave his clan explicit instructions not to embrace certain ethnic groups, I seriously doubt he'd be a willing participant of unifying the various clans of death. Especially in regards to the Samedi.</div> </div> </div> </div>And exterminated the bulk of his own clan when they explicitly wernt a threat and could have been a potential asset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T15:47:47-08:00","id":1557997,"title":"","content":"That's nothing new Saga as companies like this will listen to fan reaction and speculation and plan accordingly or change things when they see a good thing. I remember that on Buffy Season 2 that James Marsters character of Spike was going to be gone in a couple of espiodes but they listened and saw fan reactions on how good Spike was and James Marsters chemistry with the cast and decided to keep him around","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T15:52:03-08:00","id":1557998,"title":"","content":"I totally see that Augustus was an unwillingly sacafrice and it was hinted at in Cult of The Blood Gods where we have a Giovanni member venting her anger at how close minded the clan leadership were and why they supported the change with the other factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-29-2026, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T16:14:15-08:00","id":1558003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557998#post1557998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally see that Augustus was an unwillingly sacafrice and it was hinted at in Cult of The Blood Gods where we have a Giovanni member venting her anger at how close minded the clan leadership were and why they supported the change with the other factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Augustus isn't a true 3rd generation. He only succeeded in absorbing half of Cappadocious' power, which makes him the weakest of the clan founders.<br /> <br /> During the Gehenna scenario, he's actually one of the first Antes the players have an opportunity to kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T07:53:07-08:00","id":1558070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557540#post1557540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 on the other hand approached from a different, in that Goratrix was already claimed during the <i>Dark Ages</i> that he was, in fact, Tremre having been forced outside his body after he was possessed by Saulot and that the thing that the Clan served is Saulot either struggling with the Eldest, who gain acces t othe body thanks to the Vicissitude &quot;infection&quot; or Saulot already dual mind, and Saulot the &quot;Noble&quot; /Hun battled with Saulot the Evil /P'o/Beast untill they split phisically and one part &quot;Good Saulot&quot; wandered away and Evil Saulot remained behind as the White Worm of Vienna (to be fair, not a feat, considering the level 2 power of the Cultivation Discipline called Cleave the Demon allows the Kuei-jin separates his P'o from his Hun, leaving the other part of the soul in spirit form... from that materialze the other part is not that hard or find a body...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, there has long been the idea that Tremere intended for Goratrix to defect to the Sabbat, as a way to hedge to his bets (<i>Clanbook Tremere</i>, p. 21, and <i>Clanbook Tremere Revised</i>, p. 42). It's possible that V20's take stems from this, but takes it further\u2014putting Tremere in Goratrix's body from the beginning, rather than just asking Goratrix to join the Sabbat on his behalf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Tremere fell from gray eminences to personae non gratae in many regions. Without the strict internal hierarchy, individual Tremere compete heavily for the lore, artifacts, and secrets that the united Clan once possessed, fearing their clanmates as much as their enemies. To this end, they often sell their services as mercenaries to third parties. Their former monolithic structure has splintered into several rival groups, with the Camarilla-loyalists under Karl Schrekt at the head on the one side, a resurgent House Goratrix on the other, and the upstarts of House Carna who are at least for the time being still aligned with the Camarilla. A fourth house, Ipsissimus, can be found among the Anarchs.<br /> As for their Antediluvian?<br /> It was never a factor and the Second Inquisition was not even aware there was on in Vienna - or for that matter? Anyone else. Just rumors.<br /> Well except Goratrix and Tremere himself or as a bonus Saulot who god knows where at the moment. And maybe the Eldest. But since the last two are not tied to a body they are off the list - but a good option some of them orchastreted the whole thing playing the SI like a fidle.<br /> If you look closely the Second Inquisition cleared out many - in the eyes of the Camarilla - problematic persons. Or just ended ancient grudges or finished long term plans like with the case of Mithras.<br /> The point is the Sabbat not really knew for certain Tremere bit the dust and there are one less big bad around<br /> Nor the fate of Augustus is common knowledge. Or secret knowledge for thta matter </div> </div> </div>That would make the most sense. But not having the SI blitz Vienna in the first place would have been more believable. If they wanted to cut the head off the Tremere, just have the White Worm eat a bunch of them, so the survivors have to seal the chantry off as a giant magical boobytrap. This would strain credibility much less than having intelligence agencies bomb a major European city and ally.<br /> <br /> Though, a fragmented Clan Tremere is a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From the Sabbat point of view Humans became problematic and killed a bunch of Elders<br /> Witch would be good if the Sabbat wouldn't be an owergrown Anarch branch, based on personal gurdges - and not philosophy<br /> And of course if the upper and middle achelons of the Sabbat hierarchy hadn't been made up of Elders...<br /> The absolute core of the Sabbat was really three coteries: the Conspiracy of Lugoj Blood-Breaker (Sascha, Velya, Lambach, etc.); the Conspiracy of Gratiano de Verontesse (Gratiano, other Lasombra), and the Furies of Tyler (Patricia Bolingbroke). By the Convention of Thorns, these three cores had attracted a good number of ambitious vampires<br /> Now lets put aside, even the fledgelings who helped to found the Sabbat now around 500 years old - the leaders and founders?<br /> Yeah, thick blooded Elders with <i>grudges - every one of them. </i>Myca, Lamback, Velya, Gratioano, Tyler. They simply had enough on the personal level, it was not out of their good heart for a better world....<br /> Lambach, Radu, Velya, Vykos, Rustovich, Mon\u00e7ada... yeah they are Big names and even bigger Elders. Most of them were Elders and old as dust to begin with and since then just got older<br /> <br /> Some pretty key reinforcements to the Sabbat came later, the support of the Unconquered (1496); the support of the Black Hand (17th century?); the defection of House Goratrix (18th century); the defection of Melinda Galbraith (17th century)<br /> But those again, were Elders with personal grudges </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the main problem with Sabbat was the fact it was never about ideology, it was about grudges and defiance </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like the Tzimisce and the Lasombra jumping shit at the moment the Sabbat - that was nothing more basically just a tool to wage wars against their gurdges </div> </div> </div>This is a massive oversimplification. There are also some timeline issues here.<br /> <br /> The Black Hand joined shortly before or after the Convention of Thorns, in most accounts. In <i>Transylvania Chronicles II</i>, Karif is said to have joined the Sabbat at its founding and subsequently became one of the first members of the Black Hand (p. 89). I think it's fair to say the Black Hand stems from the Anarch\u2013Assamite alliances that were popping up at the time.<br /> <br /> <i>Caine's Chosen</i> suggests Dastur Anosh got the Lost Tribe involved even earlier, after hearing about the planned diablerie of Gratiano. That may be the usual unreliable narrator stuff, but p. 16 of that book does give an OOC breakdown of the diverse groups who founded the early Sabbat\u2014including the Cainite Heresy <i>and</i> a large number of Gehenna cults. These can't easily be dismissed as &quot;grudges&quot;, and they contradict your claim that this wasn't about philosophy or ideology, since that's a big part of what cults are about. Not all of these cults felt the same way, either. Add in the Black Monastery and the Inquisition, and there's clearly a strong strain of Cainite mysticism within the sect that would have had no other home (the Camarilla requiring everyone to follow Humanity).<br /> <br /> Another timeline issue: Clan Tremere only <i>confirmed</i> House Goratrix's defection to the Sabbat in the 18th century, but Goratrix's descendents apparently sided with the anarchs in 1465 (<i>Transylvania Chronicles II</i>, p. 112). They specifically did so to get protection from the main clan. The Tremere <i>antitribu</i> were also crucial in sharing the Ritual of the Bitter Rose with the anarchs and Assamites, which allowed an entire pack to gain the benefits of diablerising a single individual (p. 120). This was, then, also about opportunism (diablerie) and politics (protection and power).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of all, most of the leadership themselves at the pint sported a hefty 1000 yeras or not more behind their backs and second, most of them suspected the whole Antediluvian-killing was not a great idea to begin with (I mean just take Vykos! They personally gave birth/carried the essence of the Dracon and experienced how hard to kill these things or more like borderline impossible) </div> </div> </div>That's not evidence that they didn't think it was a good idea to kill the Antediluvians. That's just evidence that some of them know it's hard to pull off. But even accepting that some elders probably think this\u2014of course they do, just as some Camarilla elders probably fear the Ancients even while saying they don't exist\u2014that doesn't mean they think the Antediluvians <i>aren't a problem</i>. Many individuals joined the Sabbat because they knew the Ancients were real and the Camarilla had/has its eyes closed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a side note, lots of them were Nodist to begin with and anywone who read the Book of Nod noticed the one thing Caine never was a big fan of is kin-slaying<br /> Heck if you take the Erciyes Fragments he even handed out the Generation-lowering with each Embrace to make sure the younger ones will be ALWAYS weaker than the Older ones... trying to hack and slash your way thrugh his grandchildren, no matther how he hated them was basically against his wishes... </div> </div> </div>1. The Sabbat isn't just about slaying Antediluvians. It's also about preparing for Gehenna, or avoiding Gehenna, depending on who you ask. It's also about serving Caine. So the idea that the majority of its members would up and go to the Middle East also ignores this.<br /> <br /> 2. The <i>Book of Nod </i>is a contested document. Few Cainites will have read Aristotle's version, and even fewer will have read the <i>Erciyes Fragments</i>. Scholars can't even agree on which texts belong in the Book or not. So this wouldn't necessarily be known by many Sabbat members.<br /> <br /> 3. Hypocrisy is sort of the point. Cainites are hypocritical by nature. They're also kin-slayers by default. That's part of the legacy of Caine's Curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The moment the Gehenna War the fanatics molded the Sabbat from a comfortable \u201cdo as you like\u201d to a \u201cthose who are not with as are against as\u201d attitude and demanded that every true Sabbat has to march with them in their war against the Antedeluvian and other old vampires and the Sect degenerated basically a mindless swarm of locusts, giving up clan identity, completely turning from humanity, and went to war in full force with the same effectiveness as World War I. tactics of sending wave after wave of soldiers to attack the nigh untouchable Machine Gunners on ridges, the Amici Noctis clearly saw that now was the time to leave and anyone who stayed just proved they lack the survival instinct that defined their Clan - also <i>failed</i> - and the Tzimsice, so attached to their domains and gians fled with them (for some reason to the Anarch and not the neo-feudal Camarilla... but it is a whole different topic) </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the Sabbat only became a &quot;mindless swarm of locusts&quot; because that's what V5 decided. In reality, this might have killed off the shovelheads and Crusaders, but the other two thirds would have shrugged and said, &quot;Good riddance.&quot; But they could easily have decided not to do this, and then it would have been a moot point. I don't think this is necessarily more &quot;logical&quot; than simply not doing this in the first place.<br /> <br /> A more reasonable situation, flowing from BJD, would be that the Sabbat falls to civil war, giving players a lot more conflict to deal with, perhaps with one faction going to wage the Gehenna Crusade in the east. They'd probably lose some territory, but not all, and there would be enough to retain cities like Mexico and Montreal. After all, why would someone with a comfortable domain in Montreal go all the way to the Middle East to get munched down by Antediluvians? It's silly. They wouldn't. They'd still have more than enough to deal with on their own turf.<br /> <br /> As for the Ministry, I also think the name &quot;Mesu Bedshet&quot; would have been better. I didn't mind the new approach they've taken, but I would have made it less anaemic. The Hecata I like, though. There were already multiple factions of Harbingers in V20, who seemed to have different goals, so having some of them willing to join up with the Giovanni in exchange for getting rid up Uncle Auggie seems plausible enough. I think it helped that BJD really sold this idea well. What I liked less was Oblivion as a Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T22:55:21-08:00","id":1558089,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the Sabbat falling into a series of internal conflicts and it's how we dealt with them in our game of why for all intents and purposes ceased to exist as an organization and the remaining members are part of decaying war bands that are being hunted down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T07:43:56-08:00","id":1558091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558089#post1558089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of the Sabbat falling into a series of internal conflicts and it's how we dealt with them in our game of why for all intents and purposes ceased to exist as an organization and the remaining members are part of decaying war bands that are being hunted down.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the mindless, blood crazed, &quot;let's get wasted&quot; Sabbat were never truly considered members of the sect. Those were shovelheads, which were used as shock troopers to throw against the enemy and keep them distracted. The true Sabbat were far more organized and tactical in their operations. If they weren't, then they couldn't have a hierarchy of Bishops, Templars, or a black ops. division like the Black Hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T10:16:40-08:00","id":1558095,"title":"","content":"In our game we had the leadership of the Sabbat learn that they never &quot;killed&quot; Lasombra or Tzmisce at all and were demolarized by that fact and we went further and went with the notion that many of the antidivlians were no longer active participants in undead society or posing as much younger and weaker kindred and doing their own things that interested them.<br /> <br /> Some of the Sabbat leaders followed the way of Frey Diego and looked back nostalgic about their younger nights and longed to return to that and became part of the Camarilla, Anarchs or plain Autakris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-04-2026, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T17:45:46-08:00","id":1558103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558095#post1558095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In our game we had the leadership of the Sabbat learn that they never &quot;killed&quot; Lasombra or Tzmisce at all and were demolarized by that fact and we went further and went with the notion that many of the antidivlians were no longer active participants in undead society or posing as much younger and weaker kindred and doing their own things that interested them.<br /> <br /> Some of the Sabbat leaders went they way of Frey Diego and looked back nostalgic about their younger nights and longed to return to that and became part of the Camarilla, Anarchs or plain Autakris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lasombra and Tzimisce might still be around, but as the OP said, there are at least 4 Antes who have bitten the dust.<br /> <br /> Ravnos, Tremere, Saulot, Augustus.<br /> <br /> Killing one of them is a miracle. Killing two of them is Legendary. But killing 4? Well, at that point, you've just confirmed the fact that even the gods are not invincible, so long as you are sufficiently motivated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-04T00:58:49-08:00","id":1558110,"title":"","content":"By my count two of those aren't necessarily thought of as destroyed, three of them haven't been confirmed OOC, and the one who is both confirmed OOC and commonly believed to be gone was taken out by forces mysterious to Western vampires during a massive &quot;natural&quot; disaster. That doesn't sound like much of a morale boost to Sabbat members planning the resistance/uprising against the antediluvians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-04T01:29:07-08:00","id":1558111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558110#post1558110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By my count two of those aren't necessarily thought of as destroyed, three of them haven't been confirmed OOC, and the one who is both confirmed OOC and commonly believed to be gone was taken out by forces mysterious to Western vampires during a massive &quot;natural&quot; disaster. That doesn't sound like much of a morale boost to Sabbat members planning the resistance/uprising against the antediluvians.</div> </div> </div> </div>A win is a win. The main point being that as far as we are aware right now, they've been taken off the board.<br /> <br /> And with how 5th edition is trying to keep things at street level, and treating the Gehenna War like background noise, I'm inclined to believe they won't be coming back into the story any time soon, if at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-04T17:42:06-08:00","id":1558117,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't discount it yet Great Horned Ratkin that people who own VTM will not deal with the ongoing metaplot at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-04T21:42:32-08:00","id":1558119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558117#post1558117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't discount it yet Great Horned Ratkin that people who own VTM will not deal with the ongoing metaplot at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll see. Though it was my understanding the meta plot for WoD became so utterly convoluted, that it was nearly impossible to keep track of. That's why we had an End Times scenario in the first place, so we could wrap everything up, and then reboot it with Chronicles.<br /> <br /> <br /> They've already introduced so many massive retcons to the setting in 5th edition, that it's not even recognizable from the game it once was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T13:11:24-08:00","id":1558120,"title":"","content":"I tend to run lasombra as dead. Having all of them untouchable is boring and lasombras most interesting trait was that he died anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T14:05:11-08:00","id":1558121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558120#post1558120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having all of them untouchable is boring</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I respectfully disagree. As somebody who passionately dislikes the kind of world the Technocratic Union is trying to create, I'm against any of the scenarios where humanity survives the coming storm, while all the supernaturals get purged.<br /> <br /> If the world is going to end, I'd prefer that it results in mutual destruction, at the very least. Hence why I tend to go with the God's Crucible ending.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite changes in Chronicles, is that there's no doomsday clock, or Curse of Generations to worry about. The supernaturals have always been around, and shall continue to be so for the indefinite future. Heck, we even have multiple 'first generation' vampires, who were embraced without a sire; such as Longinus, or Dracula.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T17:08:02-08:00","id":1558125,"title":"","content":"One of the Antedeluvians getting killed hardly means that they can all be defeated with humanity coming through the end unscathed. There's enough of them, and they're powerful enough, that two or three going on a rampage at the same time could easily doom humanity, let alone what might happen if ten of them all started be active at the same time. Being down one just means there's a chance they can be defeated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T18:00:34-08:00","id":1558128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558125#post1558125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the Antedeluvians getting killed hardly means that they can all be defeated with humanity coming through the end unscathed. There's enough of them, and they're powerful enough, that two or three going on a rampage at the same time could easily doom humanity, let alone what might happen if ten of them all started be active at the same time. Being down one just means there's a chance they can be defeated.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they're not down just one.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos</b> - Dead after the Week of Nightmares.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere</b> - Dead by the SI, killed as effortlessly as if he were a common vampire.<br /> <br /> <b>Saulot</b> - Died with Tremere, as they were fighting for the same body.<br /> <br /> <b>Augustus</b> - Missing in action, but I choose to assume he's dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Troile</b> - Trapped in permanent Torpor after the fall of Carthiage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Five out of thirteen antedeluvians all wiped off the board at this point in the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T18:15:44-08:00","id":1558129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558128#post1558128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they're not down just one.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos</b> - Dead after the Week of Nightmares.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere</b> - Dead by the SI, killed as effortlessly as if he were a common vampire.<br /> <br /> <b>Saulot</b> - Died with Tremere, as they were fighting for the same body.<br /> <br /> <b>Augustus</b> - Missing in action, but I choose to assume he's dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Troile</b> - Trapped in permanent Torpor after the fall of Carthiage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Five out of thirteen antedeluvians all wiped off the board at this point in the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't Tremere in Goratrix's body and Saulot (his hun) on Stephan (Hunedoara)?<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T18:20:01-08:00","id":1558130,"title":"","content":"If you're counting Saulot and Tremere, than you'd need to count them as one, or call it fourteen. Tremere &quot;stole&quot; the spot from Saulot (which also undermines the idea that they need to be untouchable). You're also saying two that aren't officially completely impossible to wake up and cause problems as if they are. &quot;I chose to assume he's dead,&quot; and one being in torpor doesn't really make for a strong point on the general threat of some of them waking up and the devastation that would cause.<br /> <br /> If the count is Lasombra, Ravnos, and Tremere/Saulot as 3 out of 13... that's more of them active than you just posited (though most counts assume Ventrue is dead too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T19:12:23-08:00","id":1558131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558129#post1558129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't Tremere in Goratrix's body and Saulot (his hun) on Stephan (Hunedoara)?<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe pre-V5, but they changed a shit load of stuff around now.<br /> <br /> As far I know, the SI bombed the Vienna chantry and destroyed Tremere's body, which shattered the pyramid.<br /> <br /> Considering Tremere jumping bodies in the original meta plot did not affect the Tremere's magic or power structure, I'm inclined to believe he's been properly destroyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T19:29:40-08:00","id":1558132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558130#post1558130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're counting Saulot and Tremere, than you'd need to count them as one, or call it fourteen. Tremere &quot;stole&quot; the spot from Saulot (which also undermines the idea that they need to be untouchable). You're also saying two that aren't officially completely impossible to wake up and cause problems as if they are. &quot;I chose to assume he's dead,&quot; and one being in torpor doesn't really make for a strong point on the general threat of some of them waking up and the devastation that would cause.<br /> <br /> If the count is Lasombra, Ravnos, and Tremere/Saulot as 3 out of 13... that's more of them active than you just posited (though most counts assume Ventrue is dead too).</div> </div> </div> </div>All they had to do was spread some salt around the land, and Troile became magically bound in torpor for all time. The only way he's coming back into the story, is if somebody manages to find where he's buried and dig him out of the ground. But these are vampires we're talking about. Nobody is going to come to his rescue, unless they plan to eat him.<br /> <br /> Saulot could have very easily destroyed Tremere if he wanted to. But he literally did not even try to fight back. He just looked at Tremere from the corner of his third eye and smiled as he was devoured. Then, Tremere spent the next 1,000 years slipping in and out of consciousness, desperately trying to fight off the influence of Saulot and Tzimisce from within his own mind.<br /> <br /> Saulot is a straight up Jujutsu Sorcerer at the time of Gehenna. During the God's Crucible ending, he confronts The Eldest and drags him inside his own soul to be smote out of existence by the power of God. The same Eldest, who has spent the last 20,000 or so years systematically infecting all biological life on the planet with his mastery of Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> <br /> But you're talking about the Antedeluvians as if they're still asleep. When this topic is meant to address a concern regarding 5th edition. The Antes are awake and active. That's kind of the whole premise of The Beckoning summoning all the elders off to the middle east, to join them on the front lines.<br /> <br /> 5th edition takes place during the events of Gehenna, but is treating the situation as something happening way off in the background, where players don't have to think about it. Even dropping hints that Gehenna itself might be cyclical in nature, and that this isn't the first time the Antes have purged their bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T20:21:31-08:00","id":1558133,"title":"","content":"You're bouncing around between pre-V5 and V5 material too... so trying to say the thread is just about V5 is fairly hard to take seriously.<br /> <br /> The V5 stuff is not as internally consistent as you're saying... and nothing you're saying really matters to the idea that vampires took out some of the Antes in the past. The issue that the SI could do the damage they did? Yeah, that's a problem for the narrative of the game, but that wasn't what I responded to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T22:43:33-08:00","id":1558134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558121#post1558121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I respectfully disagree. As somebody who passionately dislikes the kind of world the Technocratic Union is trying to create, I'm against any of the scenarios where humanity survives the coming storm, while all the supernaturals get purged.<br /> <br /> If the world is going to end, I'd prefer that it results in mutual destruction, at the very least. Hence why I tend to go with the God's Crucible ending.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite changes in Chronicles, is that there's no doomsday clock, or Curse of Generations to worry about. The supernaturals have always been around, and shall continue to be so for the indefinite future. Heck, we even have multiple 'first generation' vampires, who were embraced without a sire; such as Longinus, or Dracula.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not interested in the worlds destruction in game, i disliked all the gehenna scenarios. Im interested in the 3rd gen as characters and with complex histories and actions, with that in mind the most interesting thing about lasombra was he died and his own clan killed him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T22:55:41-08:00","id":1558135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558128#post1558128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they're not down just one.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos</b> - Dead after the Week of Nightmares.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere</b> - Dead by the SI, killed as effortlessly as if he were a common vampire.<br /> <br /> <b>Saulot</b> - Died with Tremere, as they were fighting for the same body.<br /> <br /> <b>Augustus</b> - Missing in action, but I choose to assume he's dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Troile</b> - Trapped in permanent Torpor after the fall of Carthiage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Five out of thirteen antedeluvians all wiped off the board at this point in the story.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Ravnos</b> - In V5, suprisingly, it is nut sure. I mean there is &quot;<b>Blood of Zapathasura</b>&quot; - Thick, <b>sentient</b> ropes of his vitae stained the ground in Bangladesh where he fell. The noonday sun <b>did not destroy it all</b>. You own a small vial containing the Blood of the Ravnos Antediluvian. What you do with this vitae is up to you, and what it does to anyone who imbibes it is up to the Storyteller.&quot; - His sentinent (heart)blood... also, it is not really a common knowledge, not even the Ravnos actually know, except the Kuei-jin - who are not really a thing in V5 - who awoke and rampaged there <br /> <br /> <b>Tremere</b> - Again, it is not sure he was destroyed, the Pyramid not shattered because of his body, as I wrote above the Tremere were not bound to Hi, but the Seven and the upper achelon got destroyed. But even if the White Worm/Tremere Body got destroyed, again, no one really know, not even the Sabbat tremere it happened<br /> <br /> <b>Saulot</b> - See above just bit added bonuses, like a few of him waltzing around, but the common knowledge is he died in the dark ages and the Salubri around say the same, he is dead by the Tremere - and io and behold, that feat not realy gave them any special sabbat points or place <br /> <br /> <b>Augustus</b> - You might chose he is dead, but no one knows, and even if he is dead, from the Sabbat point of view this whole discussion bloomed, basically irrelevant, since a, he was like their own Gratiano, B, like with the Tremere, not provided the Giovanni any special Sabbat point of treatment for killing one Antediluvian. <br /> <br /> <b>Troile</b> - This is whole more complicated than it sounds, but let assume the Sabbat actually know Troile was in Carthage and the Followers of Set not excavated her/him like it is strongly suggested. Or you know, know who the hell Troile was... even putting aside the strong baali influence (it is Cybelle's ritual that keeps them underground not the salt) the fate of Troile would be anti-propaganda for the sabbat. because the Malkav, Gangrel, Ventrue and Troeador team offed the Antediluvian with their proto-camarilla of Rome, not some upstart Anarch rebel band; any sane Sabbat hearing this would ponder, okay, they killed one Antediluvian in a few short punic whars... we are tiptoing around over five centuries... what the actual f...???<br /> <br /> <br /> But as Heavy said, you are a bit jumping all ower with the editions.. chose one and focus on that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T01:40:32-08:00","id":1558136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558135#post1558135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Ravnos</b> - In V5, suprisingly, it is nut sure. I mean there is &quot;<b>Blood of Zapathasura</b>&quot; - Thick, <b>sentient</b> ropes of his vitae stained the ground in Bangladesh where he fell. The noonday sun <b>did not destroy it all</b>. You own a small vial containing the Blood of the Ravnos Antediluvian. What you do with this vitae is up to you, and what it does to anyone who imbibes it is up to the Storyteller.&quot; - His sentinent (heart)blood... also, it is not really a common knowledge, not even the Ravnos actually know, except the Kuei-jin - who are not really a thing in V5 - who awoke and rampaged there</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the possibility that Ravnos may have actually faked his death. Remember, he was a master of Chimerstry; which at his level was capable of producing illusions so powerful, you effectively warped reality itself. The guy was the closest thing to an Awakened Vampire as you could possibly get.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T10:50:59-08:00","id":1558144,"title":"","content":"I think that a fragment of Ravnos surviving the Week of Nightmares is a good idea and according to the lore sheet you can use the sentient vitae as you see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T15:29:33-08:00","id":1558149,"title":"","content":"There's only one thing you can do when presented with an opportunity like that.<br /> <br /> Use it to mass embrace as many people as possible, then diablerize your way down the generations.<br /> <br /> A vial of preserved, functional vitae from a clan founder is like finding the holy grail among vampires.<br /> <br /> Only a drooling imbecile would waste it on something like research, or blood sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T00:32:45-08:00","id":1558158,"title":"","content":"Well...<br /> The Vitae must flow directly from the sire to the childe.<br /> It cannot be placed in an intermediary vessel or otherwise delayed, because its supernatural properties quickly decay after leaving the vampire's body.<br /> However... there are exceptions<br /> <br /> One of the best known is Cappadocius, who was not even present when Augustus was embraced, Japeth and Constancia used his vitae in a clay jar that later become the True Vesseal<br /> Considering the Cappadocians had a ritual to preserve blood, they may have used some form of ritual magic to prepare the vitae (as a side note, the Ventrue Antediluvian said to stored in his lost fortress - among many thing, like a claw of Fenris and other funny things - a pot filled with Caine's vitae... )<br /> <br /> The other lesser known is the Baali Embrace<br /> The Baali drains his or her victim to near death and tosses him or her into the pit. In just one of the corpses the Baali hid their blood inside one of the corpses' heart. If the victim manages to find the heart before they die and drink the blood, they are considered worthy of becoming Baali. Ironically, this makes the Baali the only clan that regularly gives their victim the choice of becoming a vampire or choosing to die.<br /> Still the Baali, while present, parted with his vitae and hid it; the organ pit, the coprses, the heart preparation... The Embracing ritual of the Baali is one of their most disturbing rituals and it takes time<br /> <br /> Both cases magic is probably involved (or if you take the Ashur was the Baali progenitor, and Ashur = Cappadocius, then it could be the unique trait of his blood, the result of the touch of the Underwolrd or basically anything)<br /> <br /> With the <b>Blood of Zapathasura</b>? Well it state it is thick, <b>sentient</b> ropes vitae, maybe, perhaps, probably &quot;him&quot;; ol' Zapatashura became Venom... and probably it is his Heartblood<br /> <br /> Not many diableirised a 4th or 3rd Generation and remained mentally intact however<br /> I think - I could be wrong - there is no recorded, canon act of Amaranth (well maybe the first when a Children of Haqim ate Amarantha) when the consumed not took control in a form or another or outright survived<br /> Maybe Minos? Tho' one could argue Helena changed after she ate her sire<br /> And Yezidian refugees from the remains of the Aral Sea refer to the force of ontological evil as &quot;<i>Minos, who is the son of Arikel</i>&quot;, who rests deep within the salt flats of the dried out sea. They believe that, when &quot;<i>the other Eye opens</i>&quot;, this force of evil will rise again. This implies that Minos, or another being that assumed his identity, is apparently still active in some form.\u200b<br /> Arakur of Ur was diablerized by his own childe Lantla who was being controlled by the demon Drakonskyr, who later became Tiamat, but since Drakonskyr already set up a shop inside Lantla's soul and mind I think Arakur not really had any chance in that case<br /> <br /> Even Troile and Ilyes is questionable<br /> <br /> A bit of side tangent, but in the Second City, He had the reputation of being cold and passionless, Troile - whose gender is ambiguous, was known for being a passionate and fiery person, in stark contrast to that of their sire - Troile was Embraced by the &quot;Learned&quot;, sometime around 3000 BCE.<br /> According to the Tzimisce Clanbook, Mekhet was a sibling of the Eldest (and thus possibly another childe of Ynosh/Enoch) who, with the Brujah antediluvian &quot;played shadow games with mortals, delighting in their own cunning and agendas&quot;<br /> \u200bThere is a little inconsistency In DAV: Road of Humanity, the Prodigals told of a story in which Arikel and Troile were troubled by the way the Cainites of the <i>First City</i> behaved, and turned to Saulot for aid. The Healer stated that only empathy would help them retain a link to humanity and so, both Troile and Arikel went to work on a project of art that spanned a hundred and one years, before they brought it before Caine. The work inspired exactly those emotions within the audience that they had inspired in the mortal population. Caine was deeply touched by it and called Arikel and Troile to his side, forgiving them past trespasses. These prodigals hold this as the origin of the Road of Humanity<br /> That is not really a question, Troile was Embraced in the Second City, so the Troile in the First City was porbably Ilyes - Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand and Gehenna refer to Troile as female, suggesting that Her Sire was in love with her, but could not express it as he knew not how to deal with his emotions.<br /> It actually fits nicely in the whole picture<br /> At first, back in the old days, Ilyies and Arikel had a working relationship, so to speak, both interested in Mortals.As well as he had a working relationship with Mekhet, whom he &quot;played shadow games with mortals, delighting in their own cunning and agendas&quot; - from a Vulcan-like cold and passionate point of view this could mean experiments, cruel and cold social experiments and so on; the; the project of art that spanned a hundred and one years coud be from his early days, when he was freshly Embraced and still had that spark in him... and gradually lost it. But trusted Sualot enough to turn to him with his concerns.<br /> Ilyies was allegedly slain by his childe, Troile, who may have committed diablerie on him in the process BUT some Brujah, such as a commentator on the Erciyes Fragments, believe that his death was a lie spread by the Ventrue.<br /> In Gehenna's &quot;general description&quot; some stories, however, claim that Troile and [Brujah] had been the same person, as few to no records exist that place them together, and that [Brujah] faked his own destruction and assumed Troile's identity. (also in Gehenna the scenario &quot;Fair is Foul&quot; reintroduces Brujah to the childer of Caine under the name of Ilyes. Here, Ilyes faked his own death; having complete mastery over time, he escaped his destruction, using his trademark Discipline, Temporis,)<br /> Clanbook: Brujah Revised mentions records claiming Troile had no gender or changed it on whim.<br /> <br /> When he is not escaped via Temporis, peronally I tend to go with the later version; a bit headcanon, but could work. So, Embrace, especially Embracing your lover was a direct violation of Caine's dictum. Because of Ilyes's lack of emotion - or more precisely, he could not express his love as he knew not how to deal with his emotions - Troile feared that her Sire had the intention to destroy them, in an attempt to rectify his mistake of Embracing progeny. Thus, Troile paniced and attacked his Sire. Who consumed Her. And the act shattered his already unstable mind and assumed Her identity. A bit of reverse Mithras-Monthy-way. This would explain why Troile wasn't punished with final death for the Diablerie. It not happened. The others looked the confused and bloody mouthed Ilyies and pitied him, who began to pretend he was Troile. Even some crossdressing could have been in play. The &quot;had no gender or changed it on whim&quot; part could be viewed as the vampire basically genderlessness, since they are dead bodies, like Angels, basically have no gender, just gender identity.<br /> From there, he was Troile<br /> <br /> The official version according to clan Ventrue members states that theri Antediluvian may have been destroyed outside of the walls of the Second City by the Brujah antediluvian... which is firmly denied by the Brujah Clan. So probably it not really happened, since the Venture Antediluvian was Embracing left and right later on...<br /> <br /> Sorry, back to the original topic, so eating that blood maybe would be a mistake and probably not really usable to Embrace<br /> But then again, if it is his sentinet heartblood, basically him in a new liquid form? Maybe?<br /> Would be a good idea?<br /> No<br /> Absolutely not\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T03:35:51-08:00","id":1558159,"title":"","content":"If the vitae of Ravnos was ingested by a Kindred I would go with the notion that we have a restored antidivlian and it would mess with the Sabbat minds so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T04:26:07-08:00","id":1558161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558158#post1558158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not many diableirised a 4th or 3rd Generation and remained mentally intact however<br /> I think - I could be wrong - there is no recorded, canon act of Amaranth (well maybe the first when a Children of Haqim ate Amarantha) when the consumed not took control in a form or another or outright survived</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because they were eating ancient and experienced 4th generations. I'm talking about diablerizing a freshly embraced brood, who still have no idea what the heck is going on.<br /> <br /> You just need their generational potency. Anything else just poses a greater risk to the plan.<br /> <br /> Although as I was reading your post, I just had an epiphany about something. If the Baali has stored their blood inside a corpse, why doesn't that corpse rise as a vampire? The only explanation I can think of is that it's missed the timing window.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T06:55:11-08:00","id":1558162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558161#post1558161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Although as I was reading your post, I just had an epiphany about something. If the Baali has stored their blood inside a corpse, why doesn't that corpse rise as a vampire? The only explanation I can think of is that it's missed the timing window.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Baali hide their blood inside one of the corpses' heart - ; probably cut it out then filled it - , so the would be Baali while dying and drained of their blood have to not only dig thrugh fresh and old corpses filling the Pit but reach inside a body - if the said heart is in a body - and squeeze out the vitae like from a ripe orange<br /> Still, some rital and dark magic are had be at work because the vitae quickly become inert losing the capacity to Embrace - tho' making ghouls are fair play<br /> <br /> The whole thing is a bid muddy, to be honest<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T14:52:31-08:00","id":1558164,"title":"","content":"The thing with organ pits is that the bodies in them are just left there. Like, forever. Something about the pits can preserve the tissues inside (at least, that's the case with some of them\u2014see Iberia by Night for the one in Damascus).<br /> <br /> So there's nothing saying the bodies are fresh. Most likely, they find one that's nice and cold but long dead, and then cut out the heart. IIRC, the Embrace is supposed to require a body that's still warm (with a few exceptions). There's also debate about whether it just needs to be dead or if it has to also be exsanguinated. If the latter is true, then they could just find a body that isn't entirely exsanguinated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T16:27:13-08:00","id":1558167,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be to shocked if the Baali used some rituals to make the corpses last longer in their embrace ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T18:01:34-08:00","id":1558172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558164#post1558164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with organ pits is that the bodies in them are just left there. Like, forever. Something about the pits can preserve the tissues inside (at least, that's the case with some of them\u2014see Iberia by Night for the one in Damascus).<br /> <br /> So there's nothing saying the bodies are fresh. Most likely, they find one that's nice and cold but long dead, and then cut out the heart. IIRC, the Embrace is supposed to require a body that's still warm (with a few exceptions). There's also debate about whether it just needs to be dead or if it has to also be exsanguinated. If the latter is true, then they could just find a body that isn't entirely exsanguinated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the window of opportunity seems to be inconsistent. I can't remember if this was for Chronicles, or World, but some years ago I heard mention on youtube that if somebody dies within a week of ingesting vitae, they can still be embraced.<br /> <br /> I don't think the victim needs to be exsanguinated, just bled out. There's accounts of particularly vengeful sires who mutilated their childer before the embrace, since it doesn't heal pre-existing wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T05:02:08-08:00","id":1558181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558172#post1558172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember if this was for Chronicles, or World, but some years ago I heard mention on youtube that if somebody dies within a week of ingesting vitae, they can still be embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like posthumous embrace from Requiem. Though the time limit is within a week of death. The vitae can have been ingested at any point in their lifetime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T13:17:11-08:00","id":1558190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558103#post1558103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lasombra and Tzimisce might still be around, but as the OP said, there are at least 4 Antes who have bitten the dust.<br /> <br /> Ravnos, Tremere, Saulot, Augustus.<br /> <br /> Killing one of them is a miracle. Killing two of them is Legendary. But killing 4? Well, at that point, you've just confirmed the fact that even the gods are not invincible, so long as you are sufficiently motivated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but only Ravnos and Saulot are really Antediluvians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T20:02:44-08:00","id":1558198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558161#post1558161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because they were eating ancient and experienced 4th generations. I'm talking about diablerizing a freshly embraced brood, who still have no idea what the heck is going on.<br /> <br /> You just need their generational potency. Anything else just poses a greater risk to the plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with Lysander that attempting to do this with the particular vitae we're talking about as described in V5 is less likely to result in newbie 4th generation vampires ripe for eating than it is to result in a new host body or bodies for whatever's left of Zapathasura to manifest through. If I were one of the surviving Ravnos there's no way I'd do anything with even the slightest chance of triggering that scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-05T05:36:42-08:00","id":1558658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1557448#post1557448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5's plot mostly exists for railroading the game to were the writters want it to be rather than on its own merits so these sort of issues are common.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% Some of the ideas are ok, but that is a great way to put it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-05T13:58:44-08:00","id":1558668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558198#post1558198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm with Lysander that attempting to do this with the particular vitae we're talking about as described in V5 is less likely to result in newbie 4th generation vampires ripe for eating than it is to result in a new host body or bodies for whatever's left of Zapathasura to manifest through. If I were one of the surviving Ravnos there's no way I'd do anything with even the slightest chance of triggering that scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the only Ante's who sound like they could pull off a body jump like that would be The Eldest and Malkav.<br /> <br /> Maaaaybe it's possible for them to steal the first body, but not the others.<br /> <br /> <b>Side Note:</b> wasn't Ravnos a Silent Strider kinfolk before his embrace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-05T21:06:16-08:00","id":1558673,"title":"","content":"I would add that Ventrue and Lasombra could do body jumps with the Dominate or Oblivion discipline, but it would be easier with their direct childer or eldest grand childer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T15:31:46-08:00","id":1558688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558673#post1558673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would add that Ventrue and Lasombra could do body jumps with the Dominate or Oblivion discipline, but it would be easier with their direct childer or eldest grand childer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I say Eldest, because he's effectively become The Thing and now functions as a sentient virus.<br /> <br /> While Malkav has become an abstract entity who exists as the madness network.<br /> <br /> <br /> No matter how powerful his Dominate is, simply transferring his mind into another body would severely diminish Ventrue's power if the body being stolen wasn't 3rd generation.<br /> <br /> While Lasombra has pretty much abandoned his clan entirely, after realizing he didn't need them anymore and became an entity of pure shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T21:42:51-08:00","id":1558695,"title":"","content":"With the 3rd generation we could probably do the hand wave \ud83c\udf0a that issue Great Horned Ratkin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T01:54:40-08:00","id":1558725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557447-v5-s-gehenna-a-serious-oversight?p=1558668#post1558668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the only Ante's who sound like they could pull off a body jump like that would be The Eldest and Malkav.<br /> <br /> Maaaaybe it's possible for them to steal the first body, but not the others.<br /> <br /> <b>Side Note:</b> wasn't Ravnos a Silent Strider kinfolk before his embrace?</div> </div> </div> </div>In V5, though, the vitae is implied to be sentient or otherwise still unliving. That could be a function of high enough Fortitude or it could just be a function of really high blood potency. VTM does seem to have some form of blood sympathy, but in a less defined way than in VTR.<br /> <br /> I could also see Chimerstry 10 letting Ravnos rewrite reality to such a degree that it allows him to take over another's mind. A mind is, after all, founded on the combined subjective experiences that arise as a result of physical sensations. There's a reason people find prolonged sensory deprivation so psychologically damaging.<br /> <br /> This is probably because I've just rewatched the entire <i>A Nightmare on Elm Street </i>series over the last week, but I could see Ravnos doing what Freddy Krueger does in the second film\u2014where he attempts to take over Jesse Walsh's body through the liminal spaces between dream and waking. Now, whether he starts appearing as a burned up demon with quips and sunglasses like in <i>A Nightmare on Elm Street 4</i>, who can say! \ud83d\ude06<br /> <br /> Of course, just because it's theoretically not impossible also doesn't mean anyone has to do this. Ditto with letting it lower your Generation. The intent seems to be to hand you a massive plot device, allowing the ST to make things interesting for you whenever they want. Such potential conflict exists along a continuum, with &quot;I win&quot; (you become 4th Generation, etc.) at one end and &quot;game over, man&quot; (Ravnos takes over) as the extreme ends of the scale.<br /> <br /> More realistically, the outcome would be somewhere in the middle. Maybe you get a boost to Chimerstry (Obfuscate/Presence in V5 terms, or maybe a unique amalgam to represent your mastery of illusion) but start suffering from delusions? Or maybe your Blood Potency increases but whenever you're around other Ravnos, you trigger the diablerie-lust the clan showed during the Week of Nightmares? Or maybe it just removes the generational cap on Blood Potency, but you still have to buy it up normally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-08-2026, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}